# {{ driver_name }}

Linux misc platform driver generated by [drvforge](https://github.com/zmzzyyds/drvforge).

- **Compatible string:** `{{ compat }}`
- **Device node:** `/dev/{{ module_name }}`
- **Sysfs attribute:** `/sys/class/misc/{{ module_name }}/message`
- **Hardware required:** none (in-memory echo device; works on a PC or QEMU)

## What it does

1. Binds to a platform device advertised in the Device Tree as `{{ compat }}`.
2. Registers a misc character device backed by a 4 KiB in-memory buffer.
3. Data written to `/dev/{{ module_name }}` can be read back (echo semantics).
4. The same buffer is visible through the `message` sysfs attribute.

## Build requirements

```sh
# Debian/Ubuntu
sudo apt install build-essential linux-headers-$(uname -r) device-tree-compiler
```

## Build & test

```sh
make            # build {{ module_name }}.ko
make test       # build, insmod, run tools/test, rmmod
```

Manual flow:

```sh
make
sudo insmod {{ module_name }}.ko
echo "hello" | sudo tee /dev/{{ module_name }}
sudo cat /dev/{{ module_name }}
cat /sys/class/misc/{{ module_name }}/message
sudo rmmod {{ module_name }}
```

## Binding the driver to a device

Because the driver matches on `{{ compat }}`, a platform device with that
compatible string must exist.

### Option A — configfs overlay at runtime

Needs `CONFIG_OF_CONFIGFS`, which is **not in mainline** — it ships in heavier
vendor trees such as Raspberry Pi's. On a stock kernel, use Option B.

```sh
dtc -O dtb -o {{ module_name }}-overlay.dtbo -@ {{ module_name }}-overlay.dts
sudo mkdir -p /sys/kernel/config/device-tree/overlays/{{ module_name }}
sudo cp {{ module_name }}-overlay.dtbo \
    /sys/kernel/config/device-tree/overlays/{{ module_name }}/dtbo
```

### Option B — merge into the QEMU virt DTB before boot

The overlay carries its own `reg`, so merge it into a tree dumped with exactly
the machine parameters you are about to boot with: `-cpu`, `-m` and `-smp` are
baked into the tree.

```sh
qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt,dumpdtb=virt.dtb -cpu cortex-a57 -m 512 -smp 2
dtc -O dtb -o {{ module_name }}-overlay.dtbo -@ {{ module_name }}-overlay.dts
fdtoverlay -i virt.dtb -o virt-{{ module_name }}.dtb {{ module_name }}-overlay.dtbo
qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a57 -m 512 -smp 2 \
    -kernel Image -append "console=ttyAMA0" -dtb virt-{{ module_name }}.dtb
```

After binding, `dmesg` shows:

```
{{ module_name }}: registered /dev/{{ module_name }} (minor N)
```

## Installing with DKMS (survives kernel upgrades)

```sh
sudo dkms add .
sudo dkms install {{ module_name }}/1.0.0
```

## Moving into the kernel tree

1. Copy `{{ module_name }}.c to `drivers/misc/`.
2. Append the contents of `Kconfig` to `drivers/misc/Kconfig` and add
   `obj-$(CONFIG_{{ name_upper }}) += {{ module_name }}.o` to
   `drivers/misc/Makefile`.
3. Add the node to your board's `.dts` and submit
   (`scripts/checkpatch.pl --strict -g` before sending patches).

